<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Injo of Joseon</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1595–1649</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Injo was the sixteenth king of Joseon, ruling from 1623 to 1649. He came to the throne through a coup that deposed his uncle Gwanghaegun and broke with his policy of neutrality towards the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manchus">Manchus</a>. Manchu armies invaded in 1627 and again in 1636, and after a siege at the fortress of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/namhansanseong">Namhansanseong</a> Injo surrendered to the Qing emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hong-taiji">Hong Taiji</a> in 1637, bowing to him at Samjeondo, and sent his sons as hostages.</p></div>
